items.promptMarkdown:
In one session on the bakery tool you did four things:

1. renamed `fmt.js` to `format.js` and updated its imports;
2. reformatted the whole file with the project formatter;
3. changed how totals round, which changes visible output;
4. added a test that fails before change 3 and passes after it.

Which commit sequence makes the behaviour change easiest to review and to revert on its own?

solution.code:
function firstMissingEmail(records) {
  for (const record of records) {
    const email = record.email;
    if (typeof email !== 'string' || email.trim() === '') {
      return record.id;
    }
  }
  return null;
}

